3so5|n|A long, narrow boat with a high prow and stern, used in the canals of Venice. A gondola is usually propelled by one or two oarsmen who stand facing the prow, or by poling. A gondola for passengers has a small open cabin amidships, for their protection against the sun or rain. A sumptuary law of Venice required that gondolas should be painted black, and they are customarily so painted now. ; A flat-bottomed boat for freight. ; A long platform car, either having no sides or with very low sides, used on railroads.	a:3qcx,146,3;40z7,73,6;5eo7,44,3~40z7,73,6;3qcx,146,3;5eo7,44,3	v:8lop,90,3~8lop,90,3	n:a5gj,53,3;19w4,52,3~a5gj,53,3;19w4,52,3	N:58yx,73,3;a5gj,53,3;19w4,52,3;2cjg,44,3~a5gj,53,3;19w4,52,3;58yx,73,3;2cjg,44,3
